WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.569
-Did you know dad had affairs?
-Oh, for sure.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:07.373
-How?
-You could just tell.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.009
Lisa told me she saw him
kissing a white woman once.

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:13.880
-Why did I have no idea?
Why am I the last to know?

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.115
-'Cause you love them
too much.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.852
Enemies see each other better
than friends.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.857
-The hell did you give her?
-It's oxycodone.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.727
What? Knocks 'em right out.
-You gave her opioids to sleep?

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.629
-Yeah. You ever seen
a heroin addict?

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.964
Those guys take naps
standing up.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.097
-It's dangerous.

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:33.165
-Look, I'm keeping an eye
on her.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:34.434
I'm a doctor.
-So am I.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.737
-Right. Maybe if we need
to revive a sentence.

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.006
-We're back here
with Sterling K. Brown.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.275
That was a clip
from "American Fiction"

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.177
with the great Jeffrey Wright.
-Yes.

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:45.545
Amazing.
-A couple of things.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:49.181
One, I just assumed,
based on the quality of his work

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:51.417
over the years,
so consistently excellent,

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.152
Jeffrey been nominated
for an Oscar before.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.387
This is his first nomination.

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.422
-His first nomination.
-Even cooler,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.157
this is the first time
two Black actors

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.092
have been nominated for lead
and supporting in the same film.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:03.830
-Isn't that crazy?
-That's crazy and wonderful.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.398
-Yeah, like, honestly, I've been
a part of a couple of firsts,

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:07.733
and it's 2024, and I was like,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.268
this has happened already,
hasn't it?

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.370
It's like first time?
Alright, that's cool.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:12.371
-It's fun to be the first.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.772
It should have happened earlier,

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:15.408
but I guess it's nice to be --
-Not too bad.

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:18.344
-Speaking of fun,
it did seem like this is a movie

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.413
that takes
on a lot of weighty subjects,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.483
but it also feels like a film
where the cast --

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.817
because, I don't know,

00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:26.452
it's funny
how it approaches everything.

00:01:26.518 --> 00:01:27.920
It seemed like you were
all having

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.889
a very good time with it.
-Well, we had an absolute blast.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.523
I mean, we talk about
a lot of different things

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.627
in terms of representation
and sort of the narrow milieu

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.695
in terms of what Black people
are often seen in

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:40.466
and trying to expand
the breadth of representation,

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.568
but at the same time,
like it's really,

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.037
really, really funny.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.805
And when you're
having fun on set --

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.873
I'm working with my idols
with Leslie Uggams

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.475
and Jeffrey Wright,
Erika Alexander,

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.710
Tracee Ellis Ross,

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:53.846
and I just get a chance
to be silly and fun.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.149
I'm normally the dude who has
to hold [bleep] together,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.450
and in this one,
I'm a bit of a mess,

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.052
and you're like,
we got to deal with Cliff.

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:01.687
So it's fun to sort of occupy
that space.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.821
And we all had a blast.

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:04.123 align:start size:78% position:22%
-Yeah, it was nice
to actually get

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.058
to see you as the sibling
who's a mess.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:08.461
-Yeah, yeah.
-You had to do the heavy work.

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:10.429
-Randall had to hold it
together for a long time.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:13.732
Now Cliff is just like,
I don't know.

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:16.202
-I want to talk to you
about a piece of work that,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.337
based on what you've said,
you've never been asked about

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.173
on television before --
a role that I don't think

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:22.408
anybody -- when we talk
about representation

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the breadth of the roles
you're offered.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:24.844
-Talk to me.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.082
-You got to play Sia
in a Lonely Island video.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.686
-I really did.
-This was -- Yeah.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.054
-It was so much fun.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:38.090
Andy came up to me.
I shot an episode of "Nine-Nine"

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.458
and he's like, hey, man,
would you want to come

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.527
and do this Lonely Island thing?
You get to play Sia.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.128
And I was like,
how does that work?

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:44.397
And he's like, well,
I'll show you.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:45.999
You're going to lip sync
all of her stuff.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:49.402
And I was like, just -- it's
called "Silk Robes and Kimonos."

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.436
And I was like,
this sounds really dumb

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:52.705
and delightful.
-Yeah.

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:54.573
-Sign me up.
-By the way, dumb and delightful

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.744
describes everything
they've ever done.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.246
Now, this is from
the wonderful Netflix.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:02.081
I don't even call it --
I guess short.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.483
I don't even know
how you would describe

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.683
"Bash Brothers" --
-"Bash Brothers."

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.052
-Yeah, I highly recommend
watching it.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:08.087
But here, just for casting,

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.889
I would say the craziest thing
is you play Sia,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:13.459
but then Andy plays
Jose Canseco and Akiva Schaffer

00:03:13.525 --> 00:03:15.394
plays Mark McGuire.
-Yeah, it's all crazy.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.229
-Nobody's playing
who they should.

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:18.597
-No.

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:19.731
-But you know what?
You guys are all in the pocket.

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:21.367
Let's take a look
at a quick clip.

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:22.935
-Oh, man.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:26.205
-♪ Silk robes and kimonos ♪

00:03:26.271 --> 00:03:29.309
♪ Silk robes and kimonos ♪

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.377
♪ Change outta
your own clothes ♪

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.679
♪ These athletic days,
but oh, those... ♪

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.881
-♪ Oakland Nights ♪

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:39.719
-It's really good.
It's really good.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.088
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.523
-That was fun. Oh, man.
-Watching it,

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.259
it's a real, you know --
to casting directors everywhere,

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.228
just open your heart and your
mind when you're casting.

00:03:49.294 --> 00:03:50.396
-You know what I'm saying?

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.998
Don't be so narrow.
Open your mind.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:56.102
-The funniest thing was they
said we can only show 10 seconds

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:57.637
of the clip
because of music licensing.

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.272
And I'm like,
who's coming to get the money?

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:02.641
[Bleep] Samberg?
Is Samberg going to call up

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.610
and be like, "Hey, that was more
than a 10 seconds."

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.179
That's a good Samberg.
You're good.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.713
-I do a very good --
Yeah, but will they ever

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.084
cast me as Samberg?
No, no, he's going to do it.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.353
Uh, what a delight
to have you back.

00:04:14.419 --> 00:04:15.755
Congratulations on everything.
-It's a pleasure, man.

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.290
Thank you so much.
-Good luck out there.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:19.058
-Thank you, sir.
-The hard part's over.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.259
Sterling K. Brown, everyone.

00:04:20.325 --> 00:04:21.727
"American Fiction"
in theater now.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.796
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Melissa Rauch.

